From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 04:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] build.zig: define RISC-V float ABI macros for translate-c

Zig 0.16's translate-c runs on Aro, whose predefined macros for RISC-V
stop at `__riscv` and `__riscv_xlen`: it never emits `__riscv_flen` or
`__riscv_float_abi_double`, which clang and GCC define for an lp64d
target. glibc's riscv `bits/setjmp.h`, pulled in by Python.h through
pthread.h, requires one of the `__riscv_float_abi_*` macros:

    /usr/include/bits/setjmp.h:35:3: error: unsupported FLEN

so the CPython C-API translation fails and no manylinux_riscv64 wheel
can be built. musl's headers do not test these macros, so
musllinux_riscv64 builds unaffected. Reproduces on any host with
`zig translate-c -lc -target riscv64-linux-gnu`.

Zig master already emits these macros from Aro (ziglang/zig commit
b46a7f3a25a6, "sync aro & translate-c"); this is unnecessary once zttp
moves to a Zig release that contains it.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; workaround for Zig 0.16, fixed by ziglang/zig b46a7f3a25a6 on master]
---
 build.zig | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build.zig b/build.zig
index 8fdf7d7..6ee8b5c 100644
--- a/build.zig
+++ b/build.zig
@@ -149,6 +149,14 @@ pub fn build(b: *std.Build) void {
     // on the build backend to pass it - so on Windows the translation silently
     // targets the GIL ABI unless we define it here.
     if (free_threaded and target.result.os.tag == .windows) translate.defineCMacro("Py_GIL_DISABLED", "1");
+    // Zig 0.16's translate-c (Aro) predefines no RISC-V floating-point macros,
+    // so glibc's riscv bits/setjmp.h (reached via pthread.h) hits `#error
+    // unsupported FLEN`. Define what clang does for an lp64d target; Zig master
+    // already emits these itself.
+    if (target.result.cpu.arch.isRISCV() and target.result.cpu.has(.riscv, .d)) {
+        translate.defineCMacro("__riscv_flen", "64");
+        translate.defineCMacro("__riscv_float_abi_double", "1");
+    }
 
     const fixer = b.addExecutable(.{
         .name = "fix_cimport",
-- 
2.43.0

